completed the docs sync at 09:33Z, committed the operational retrospective for
.614 at 09:38Z with its artifact, and rewrote docs_audit_report.md at 09:41Z.
Zero BLOCK or FAIL rows in the 45 minutes since. The retro is one of the three
switched tiers, so a phase that could not complete on the new model completed
on the old one.

The three counter increments since the last check looked like the rollback
failing. All three fall between 09:13 and 09:28, before the restart. Counted
rather than assumed, because dashboard totals are per-day and cannot show which
side of an event a row falls on.

So the model was the cause as far as this evidence can say. It is still not a
diagnosis: why gpt-6-astra fails inside the conductor's codex wrapper while
